{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771216229643,"sessionID":"ses_39b4a6031ffeAK8YDRvg3YQ2Hi","part":{"id":"prt_c64b6d505001M5LD2E75T30Lt3","sessionID":"ses_39b4a6031ffeAK8YDRvg3YQ2Hi","messageID":"msg_c64b6c276001jQYbXpoQaWwCkG","type":"tool","callID":"call_838a233a00034a52a7759d9b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","offset":1100,"limit":300},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1100: - Prevents default behavior to avoid any conflicts\n1101: - Toggle functionality opens/closes settings panel on key press\n1102: - Follows existing pattern from useTransition.ts for keyboard handling\n1103: - All 341 tests passing\n1104: \n1105: **Technical Decisions:**\n1106: \n1107: - Uses `e.code === 'Backquote'` for key detection (consistent with existing code)\n1108: - Event listener attached to global `window` object\n1109: - useEffect with empty dependency array ensures single listener registration\n1110: - Proper cleanup removes event listener on unmount\n1111: - `e.preventDefault()` called to prevent any browser default behavior\n1112: - Simple toggle logic: `setSettingsPanelOpen((prev) => !prev)`\n1113: \n1114: **Test Coverage:**\n1115: \n1116: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1117: - Keyboard functionality verified through manual testing\n1118: - Pattern consistent with useTransition.ts keyboard implementation\n1119: \n1120: **Implementation Summary (Triple-Tap Gesture):**\n1121: \n1122: - Implemented custom hook useTripleTapGesture for mobile gesture detection\n1123: - Triple-tap detection in top-left corner (100x100px threshold)\n1124: - Configurable parameters: threshold (default 100px), maxTimeBetweenTaps (default 500ms)\n1125: - Touch and click event handling with preventDefault for touch\n1126: - Automatic state reset if too much time passes between taps\n1127: - Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n1128: - Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n1129: - All 341 tests passing\n1130: \n1131: **Technical Decisions:**\n1132: \n1133: - Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n1134: - Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n1135: - Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n1136: - Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n1137: - Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n1138: - Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n1139: - Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n1140: \n1141: **Test Coverage:**\n1142: \n1143: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1144: - Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n1145: - Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n1146: \n1147: **Implementation Summary (Export/Import JSON):**\n1148: \n1149: - Implemented Export JSON button in SettingsPanel footer\n1150: - Implemented Import JSON button with hidden file input\n1151: - Export creates downloadable JSON file (gol-expert-settings.json)\n1152: - Import loads JSON file with validation\n1153: - Comprehensive validation for all expert settings parameters\n1154: - Error message display for invalid imports\n1155: - File format: JSON with pretty-printing (2-space indentation)\n1156: - Blob-based file download with URL.createObjectURL\n1157: - FileReader API for file upload\n1158: - All 349 tests passing\n1159: \n1160: **Technical Decisions:**\n1161: \n1162: - Export uses Blob and URL.createObjectURL for download\n1163: - Pretty-printed JSON with 2-space indentation\n1164: - Import validates against all parameter ranges\n1165: - Custom validation function returns detailed error messages\n1166: - Hidden file input triggered via button click\n1167: - Error state managed in component state\n1168: - Invalid settings prevent import with user feedback\n1169: \n1170: **Validation Coverage:**\n1171: \n1172: - Movement detection: centroidHistoryLength (3-10), movementThreshold (0.1-2.0), minClusterSize (1-5)\n1173: - Scoring: moverPointsPerGeneration (1-100), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (0-20), scoreMultiplier (0.1-5.0)\n1174: - Level generation: baseTimeSeconds (10-120), timeIncrementPerLevel (0-60), baseFlux (5-50), difficultyScalingMode (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n1175: - Grid sizing: mobileCellSize (14-24), desktopCellSize (16-28), minVisibleCells (≥1)\n1176: - Audio: enabled (boolean), volume (0-0.5), waveform (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n1177: \n1178: **Test Coverage:**\n1179: \n1180: - All existing 349 tests continue to pass\n1181: - Export functionality verified through manual testing\n1182: - Import functionality verified with valid and invalid JSON files\n1183: - Error handling tested for malformed JSON\n1184: \n1185: ### 5.2 Presets System (LOW - Convenience)\n1186: \n1187: - [x] Implement preset configurations\n1188:   - Easy: Lower difficulty, generous resources\n1189:   - Normal: Balanced gameplay\n1190:   - Hard: Strict time/flux limits\n1191:   - Chaos: Extreme parameters, unpredictable\n1192: - [x] Implement preset selection UI\n1193:   - Dropdown in Expert Settings\n1194:   - Preview preset values\n1195: - [ ] Add custom preset support\n1196:   - Allow users to save current settings as preset\n1197:   - Name and save custom configurations\n1198: \n1199: **Dependencies**: Expert settings\n1200: \n1201: **Implementation Summary:**\n1202: \n1203: - Implemented Preset type in src/types/index.ts with four preset options: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS\n1204: - Implemented src/lib/presets.ts library with applyPreset(), getPresetDescription(), and preset configurations\n1205: - Created four preset configurations with balanced parameter sets:\n1206:   - EASY: Generous Flux (30), longer time limits (90s), lenient scoring (15pt movers, 3pt oscillators), lower movement threshold (0.3)\n1207:   - NORMAL: Balanced Flux (20), standard time limits (60s), standard scoring (10pt movers, 2pt oscillators), standard movement threshold (0.5)\n1208:   - HARD: Limited Flux (15), shorter time limits (40s), strict scoring (8pt movers, 1pt oscillators), higher movement threshold (0.7)\n1209:   - CHAOS: Extreme Flux (10), very short time limits (30s), chaotic scoring (5pt movers, 1pt oscillators), low movement threshold (0.1), larger grid sizing (28px desktop, 22px mobile)\n1210: - Updated SettingsPanel.tsx to include preset selector with description at top of panel\n1211: - Updated SettingsPanel.css with preset section styling\n1212: - Updated createInitialExpertSettings() in src/lib/state.ts to use NORMAL preset by default\n1213: - Added comprehensive test suite with 11 tests covering all presets and edge cases\n1214: - All tests passing (360 total)\n1215: \n1216: **Technical Decisions:**\n1217: \n1218: - Preset type defined as enum-like string union: 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n1219: - applyPreset() performs deep clone using JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) to prevent mutation issues\n1220: - getPresetDescription() returns human-readable description for each preset explaining the balance and intended difficulty\n1221: - Preset selector placed at top of SettingsPanel for easy access and visibility\n1222: - Preset descriptions use glassmorphism styling with subtle background for readability\n1223: - Default preset is NORMAL for balanced gameplay experience\n1224: - All preset parameters validated against spec-defined ranges\n1225: - Preset application immediately updates all expert settings without requiring panel close/reopen\n1226: - Preset configurations include all expert settings: movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing, and audio parameters\n1227: \n1228: **Test Coverage: 11 tests**\n1229: \n1230: - Preset type definition: 1 test\n1231: - EASY preset configuration: 1 test\n1232: - NORMAL preset configuration: 1 test\n1233: - HARD preset configuration: 1 test\n1234: - CHAOS preset configuration: 1 test\n1235: - applyPreset() deep clone behavior: 1 test\n1236: - applyPreset() applies correct values: 1 test\n1237: - getPresetDescription() returns correct descriptions: 3 tests (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS)\n1238: - Invalid preset handling: 1 test\n1239: \n1240: **Integration Notes:**\n1241: \n1242: - Presets integrated into SettingsPanel as dropdown selector at top of panel\n1243: - Preset selector onChange handler calls applyPreset() to update expert settings\n1244: - Preset descriptions displayed below selector to explain each preset's characteristics\n1245: - createInitialExpertSettings() now uses applyPreset('NORMAL') for default configuration\n1246: - Preset system works seamlessly with existing settings persistence (localStorage)\n1247: - Users can manually tweak parameters after selecting a preset for further customization\n1248: - Total test count: 360 tests passing (up from 349)\n1249: \n1250: ---\n1251: \n1252: ## Sprint 6: Quality Assurance\n1253: \n1254: _Goal: Stability, accessibility, and performance_\n1255: \n1256: ### 6.1 Error Handling & Resilience (MEDIUM - Stability)\n1257: \n1258: - [ ] Implement global error boundary\n1259:   - Catch React component errors\n1260:   - Display user-friendly error message\n1261:   - Log error details\n1262: - [ ] Add input validation\n1263:   - Validate all user inputs\n1264:   - Validate configuration parameters\n1265:   - Prevent NaN and infinity\n1266: - [ ] Handle edge cases gracefully\n1267:   - Empty grid states\n1268:   - Zero flux scenarios\n1269:   - Invalid level numbers\n1270:   - Corrupted localStorage\n1271: - [ ] Add retry mechanisms\n1272:   - Retry failed operations with exponential backoff\n1273:   - Graceful degradation when features fail\n1274: - [ ] Handle browser compatibility\n1275:   - Check for required APIs (Web Audio, Canvas)\n1276:   - Fallbacks for unsupported features\n1277:   - Clear error messages\n1278: \n1279: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1280: \n1281: ### 6.2 Accessibility (LOW - Inclusivity)\n1282: \n1283: - [ ] Implement keyboard navigation\n1284:   - Arrow keys for grid navigation\n1285:   - Enter/Space to place cells\n1286:   - Escape to cancel/close panels\n1287:   - Tab navigation through UI controls\n1288: - [ ] Add screen reader support\n1289:   - ARIA labels for UI elements\n1290:   - Announce game state changes\n1291:   - Alternative text for visual elements\n1292:   - Live regions for score/timer updates\n1293: - [ ] Implement reduced motion support\n1294:   - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query\n1295:   - Disable animations when requested\n1296:   - Simplified visual feedback\n1297: - [ ] Add high contrast mode\n1298:   - Toggle for high contrast colors\n1299:   - Larger text option\n1300:   - Improved readability\n1301: - [ ] Ensure minimum touch targets\n1302:   - 44×44px minimum for mobile\n1303:   - Spacious clickable areas\n1304: - [ ] Focus management\n1305:   - Visible focus indicators\n1306:   - Logical tab order\n1307:   - Focus trap in modals\n1308: \n1309: **Dependencies**: UI components, user interaction\n1310: \n1311: ### 6.3 Performance Optimization (LOW - Performance)\n1312: \n1313: - [ ] Implement performance monitoring\n1314:   - FPS counter (development only)\n1315:   - Memory usage tracking\n1316:   - Component render profiling\n1317: - [ ] Add performance optimizations\n1318:   - Memoize expensive calculations\n1319:   - Virtualize large lists (if applicable)\n1320:   - Lazy load non-critical components\n1321:   - Debounce/throttle frequent operations\n1322: - [ ] Profile and optimize\n1323:   - Identify performance bottlenecks\n1324:   - Optimize critical paths\n1325:   - Ensure 60fps with 500+ cells\n1326:   - Test on low-end devices\n1327: - [ ] Implement lazy loading\n1328:   - Load audio on first interaction\n1329:   - Lazy load expert settings panel\n1330:   - Code splitting for production\n1331: \n1332: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1333: \n1334: ### 6.4 Testing (LOW - Quality Assurance)